Caelza: one Mind for every device (vision M3, the shared brain's consumer
shape): the Mind that already runs on one device (usually the PC) also
listens on the owner's home-network or Tailscale address, and the other
device's Runtime joins it with a code from the Memory page, so one Cael has
one memory on the PC and the phone. No shell.

The gateway's api_mind_share.rs (an overlay module) answers
GET|POST|DELETE /api/mind/share on the device that hosts the Mind (its
addresses, the address written into the service's config.json as a
`tailnetHosts` entry, a `caelza-share` token minted into its tokens.json as
a hash, the join code) and POST /api/mind/probe on the device that joins
(the service's /health, then brain_stats with the code's token). The page
on the joining device writes the config through the upstream config API.
These hunks register the module and its routes, list the page logic test
beside the others and add a sentence to Cael's Memory screen explanation. Applied after 0015 and the
overlay copy.


